/**
 * @defgroup StFtpcSlowSimMaker StFtpcSlowSimMaker — FTPC Slow Simulator
 * @ingroup  StFtpcSlowSimMaker
 *
 * @brief Full detector simulation of the STAR Forward Time Projection
 *        Chambers (FTPC West and FTPC East), modelling every physical
 *        process from primary ionisation through to zero-suppressed ADC
 *        output in the STAR DAQ raw-data format.
 *
 * @section ftpc_physics_overview Physics Overview
 *
 * Each FTPC is a cylindrical radial-drift time-projection chamber centred
 * on the beam axis.  Charged particles produced in the STAR interaction
 * region enter the sensitive gas volume (Ar/CO₂ 50:50) and deposit energy
 * by ionisation along their path.  The liberated electrons drift
 * <em>radially outward</em> (away from the beam) under a radial electric
 * field maintained by a cylindrical cathode at inner radius \f$r_\text{in}\f$
 * and the anode wires/Frisch grid near the outer radius \f$r_\text{out}\f$.
 * On arrival at the anode, each primary electron is amplified in a
 * Townsend avalanche.  The induced charge is collected on segmented cathode
 * pads arranged in azimuthal sectors, digitised by switched-capacitor-array
 * (SCA) electronics, and shipped to the DAQ as zero-suppressed 8-bit
 * samples.
 *
 * @section ftpc_pipeline Simulation Pipeline
 *
 * The simulation proceeds in the following stages for every GEANT hit in
 * the FTPC sensitive volume:
 *
 * -# **Coordinate transform** (StFtpcSlowSimulator::simulate) \n
 *    The global GEANT hit position \f$(x,y,z)\f$ is rotated into the local
 *    FTPC coordinate system using StFtpcTrackingParams.  The FTPC row
 *    index is extracted from the GEANT volume ID.
 *
 * -# **Primary ionisation** (StFtpcSlowSimulator::simulate) \n
 *    The number of primary electrons is
 *    \f[ N_e = \frac{\Delta E}{W_i} \f]
 *    where \f$\Delta E\f$ is the GEANT energy deposit in the step and
 *    \f$W_i\f$ is the effective gas ionisation potential stored in the
 *    database (\c ftpcGas, field \c gasIonizationPotential, in eV).
 *
 * -# **Track-angle widths** (StFtpcSlowSimulator::simulate) \n
 *    The cluster is spread in the radial direction by the dip angle
 *    \f$\lambda\f$ and in the azimuthal direction by the crossing angle
 *    \f$\alpha\f$:
 *    \f[ \delta r = L_\text{pad} \tan\lambda, \qquad
 *        \delta\phi\cdot r = L_\text{pad} \tan\alpha \f]
 *    where \f$L_\text{pad}\f$ is the pad length.
 *
 * -# **Electric field grid** (StFtpcSlowSimField) \n
 *    The radial field is discretised on a uniform grid of
 *    \c numSlowSimGridPoints points from \f$r_\text{in}\f$ to
 *    \f$r_\text{out}\f$.  At each grid point the local electric field
 *    \f[ E(r) = \frac{|V_\text{cath}|}{r\,\ln(r_\text{out}/r_\text{in})} \f]
 *    is used to interpolate the drift velocity \f$v_z(E)\f$, the
 *    transverse and longitudinal diffusion coefficients
 *    \f$D_T\f$, \f$D_L\f$ (in \f$\mu\text{m}/\sqrt{\text{cm}}\f$), and
 *    the Lorentz deflection angle \f$\theta_L(E)\f$ from the slow-sim gas
 *    table (\c ftpcSlowSimGas).
 *
 *    A second, higher-resolution table of drift velocity and Lorentz
 *    angle binned by E-field and pad-row position is read from the
 *    Magboltz-derived database tables (\c ftpcVDrift, \c ftpcDeflection,
 *    \c ftpcdVDriftdP, \c ftpcdDeflectiondP) and corrected for the
 *    ambient pressure and temperature of each FTPC independently:
 *    \f[ v(E,\Delta P) = v_0(E) + \frac{dv}{dP}\Delta P, \qquad
 *        \theta_L(E,\Delta P) = \theta_0(E) + \frac{d\theta}{dP}\Delta P \f]
 *    where \f$\Delta P = P_\text{now} - P_\text{std}\f$ is the pressure
 *    deviation from standard conditions.  An optional cathode-offset
 *    correction modifies the effective inner radius as a function of
 *    azimuth \f$\phi\f$ to simulate mechanical misalignment of the inner
 *    cathode cylinder.
 *
 * -# **Drift and diffusion** (StFtpcSlowSimCluster::DriftDiffuse) \n
 *    Each cluster drifts radially outward in steps of size
 *    \f$\delta r = (r_\text{out}-r_\text{in}) / (N_\text{grid}-1)\f$.
 *    At each step:
 *    \f{align*}{
 *      \phi      &\mathrel{+}= \frac{\delta r}{r}\,\theta_L(r) \\
 *      t_\text{drift} &\mathrel{+}= \frac{\delta r}{v_z(r)}
 *    \f}
 *    Diffusion is computed every \c diffusionCoarseness steps to save
 *    CPU, accumulating
 *    \f{align*}{
 *      \sigma_r^2 &\mathrel{+}= D_L^2\,\delta r\,n_c
 *                  + \sigma_r^2\left(1 + \frac{d\ln v}{dr}\cdot 2\delta r\,n_c\right) \\
 *      \sigma_\phi^2 &\mathrel{+}= D_T^2\,n_c\,\delta r
 *                    + \sigma_\phi^2 (1+\delta r/r \cdot n_c)^2
 *    \f}
 *    where \f$n_c\f$ is the diffusion coarseness integer.  A linear
 *    electron-attachment loss \f$\epsilon\f$ per unit path (gas
 *    attenuation from the database) reduces the cluster charge each
 *    coarseness block.
 *
 * -# **Gas amplification** (StFtpcSlowSimReadout::Avalanche) \n
 *    Groups of 10 primary electrons are processed together; each group
 *    produces a Polya-distributed gain sample centred on the mean gas
 *    gain \f$G\f$ (from \c ftpcGas::gasGain):
 *    \f[ P(k) = C \left(mk\right)^{m-1} e^{-mk}, \qquad m=\tfrac{3}{2} \f]
 *    The cumulative CDF is pre-tabulated and sampled via the
 *    Locate–binary-search algorithm.
 *
 * -# **Pad-response function** (StFtpcSlowSimReadout::PadResponse) \n
 *    The azimuthal width (in \f$\mu\text{m}\f$) after including the pad
 *    response function (PRF) is
 *    \f[ \sigma_\text{pad} = \sqrt{\sigma_\phi^2 + \sigma_\text{PRF}^2} \f]
 *    The Gaussian PRF sigma \f$\sigma_\text{PRF}\f$ is stored in
 *    \c ftpcSlowSimPars::sigmaPadResponseFuntion.
 *
 * -# **Shaper-electronics response** (StFtpcSlowSimReadout::ShaperResponse) \n
 *    The drift-time width is converted to nanoseconds and convolved with
 *    the shaper FWHM \f$\tau_s\f$ (from \c ftpcSlowSimPars::readoutShaperTime):
 *    \f[ \sigma_t = \sqrt{\left(\frac{\sigma_r}{v_\text{final}}\right)^2
 *                  + \left(\frac{\tau_s}{2.355}\right)^2} \f]
 *    The factor 2.355 converts FWHM to \f$\sigma\f$ of a Gaussian.
 *
 * -# **Digitisation** (StFtpcSlowSimReadout::Digitize) \n
 *    Track-angle offsets are used to split each cluster into
 *    \f$2n_\text{sub}+1\f$ equally-weighted sub-hits along the track,
 *    where \f$n_\text{sub} = 2\sqrt{(\delta r/L_\text{pad})^2+(\delta\phi/\delta\phi_\text{bin})^2}\f$.
 *    Each sub-hit deposits charge into the floating-point ADC array
 *    \c mADCArray[row][sector][pad][timebin] by integrating the
 *    Gaussian pad and time distributions over each pad/timebin cell.
 *    A per-channel time offset from the database (\c ftpcTimeOffset) is
 *    applied before the time integration.
 *
 * -# **ADC conversion and noise** (StFtpcSlowSimReadout::OutputADC) \n
 *    Each non-zero cell is scaled by the ADC conversion factor, a
 *    per-channel gain slope (\c ftpcAmpSlope) and offset (\c ftpcAmpOffset)
 *    from the database, then smeared by Gaussian white noise of
 *    \f$\sigma=1.5\f$ ADC counts.  Cells below the zero-suppression
 *    threshold are cleared; cells above the maximum 8-bit value are
 *    clipped.
 *
 * -# **DAQ encoding** (StFtpcRawWriter::writeArray) \n
 *    The hardware pad/sector numbering differs from the simulation
 *    ordering: in the West FTPC and the outer cards of East FTPC the
 *    pad order is inverted.  After remapping, data are encoded into
 *    three STAR DAQ tables (\c fcl_ftpcndx, \c fcl_ftpcsqndx,
 *    \c fcl_ftpcadc) using a two-threshold zero-suppression scheme
 *    (high threshold 5 ADC counts, low threshold 2 ADC counts, minimum
 *    2 bins above the low threshold) and the STAR SEQD run-length
 *    encoding used by the real DAQ.
 *
 * @section ftpc_database Database Tables
 *
 * | Table                | Dataset path                           | Contents |
 * |----------------------|----------------------------------------|----------|
 * | ftpcDimensions       | Geometry/ftpc                          | Radii, number of rows/sectors/pads/timebins |
 * | ftpcAsicMap          | Geometry/ftpc                          | ASIC mapping flags |
 * | ftpcInnerCathode     | Geometry/ftpc                          | Cathode offset and angle |
 * | ftpcEField           | Calibrations/ftpc                      | Nominal cathode voltage |
 * | ftpcVDrift           | Calibrations/ftpc                      | Magboltz drift-velocity table |
 * | ftpcDeflection       | Calibrations/ftpc                      | Magboltz Lorentz-angle table |
 * | ftpcdVDriftdP        | Calibrations/ftpc                      | Drift-velocity pressure derivative |
 * | ftpcdDeflectiondP    | Calibrations/ftpc                      | Lorentz-angle pressure derivative |
 * | ftpcGas              | Calibrations/ftpc                      | Gas gain, ionisation potential, attenuation |
 * | ftpcDriftField       | Calibrations/ftpc                      | Radial field geometry |
 * | ftpcElectronics      | Calibrations/ftpc                      | t₀, microsecondsPerTimebin |
 * | ftpcAmpSlope         | Calibrations/ftpc                      | Per-channel gain slope |
 * | ftpcAmpOffset        | Calibrations/ftpc                      | Per-channel gain offset |
 * | ftpcTimeOffset       | Calibrations/ftpc                      | Per-channel time offset |
 * | ftpcTemps            | Calibrations/ftpc                      | Body temperature sensors |
 * | ftpcSlowSimGas       | ftpc (StarDb)                          | Drift/diffusion vs. E-field table |
 * | ftpcSlowSimPars      | ftpc (StarDb)                          | Simulator tuning parameters |
 * | ftpcClusterPars      | ftpc (StarDb)                          | Cluster-finder parameters |
 *
 * @section ftpc_files Source Files
 *
 * | File                         | Role |
 * |------------------------------|------|
 * | StFtpcSlowSimMaker.cxx/.h    | STAR Maker; database initialisation, per-event orchestration |
 * | StFtpcSlowSimulator.cc/.hh   | Core simulation loop over GEANT hits |
 * | StFtpcSlowSimField.cc/.hh    | Electric-field grid, drift velocity and Lorentz angle |
 * | StFtpcSlowSimCluster.cc/.hh  | Single ionisation cluster: drift, diffusion |
 * | StFtpcSlowSimReadout.cc/.hh  | Avalanche, PRF, shaper, digitisation |
 * | StFtpcSlowSimLibs.cc         | Utility: binary-search Locate() |
 * | StFtpcRawWriter.cc/.hh       | DAQ table encoder (ndx/sqndx/adc) |
 * | StFssSectorReader.cc/.hh     | Sector-level DAQ table reader |
 */

